        "field_id": "question_69061794",
        "label": "Why are you interested in this opportunity?",
        "type": "textarea",
        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:question_69061794",
        "action": "fill",
        "value": "I'm drawn to this because the work is implementation, not demo building. NISC serves 960+ energy cooperatives and communication organizations, which means analytics has to survive contact with real operators and real workflows, and that is the constraint I keep choosing. At Summer Atlantic Capital I build the machine-learning core of an anomaly-detection and alert-prioritization system, and the thing I spend most of my time on is not model accuracy. It's whether the output is actually usable: an anomaly system that fires too many alerts creates a second problem instead of solving the first, so I built a learning-to-rank layer for prioritizing alerts and a retrieval-augmented explanation layer so a human analyst can see why something surfaced. Earlier, at Intelehealth, I built a resource-availability scoring pipeline across 32 villages combining facility-tier classification, geospatial distance, and weather data, which taught me how much of operations analytics is reconciling messy inputs from different sources. I'm an Applied Math and Statistics and Economics student, so the statistical side is the part I'm formally trained in, but what I want from this internship is the implementation side: sitting with the people who use the analytics and finding out where it breaks.",
        "reason": "Essay generated from the operator's about-me context"
